# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever cloned the repo.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default, so every checkout on this machine
# rewrote LF to CRLF in the working tree. That is harmless for Python and for
# anything Windows reads -- and fatal for a shell script the moment it runs on
# Linux:
#
#     scripts/hailo_compile.sh: line 17: $'\r': command not found
#     scripts/hailo_compile.sh: line 18: set: pipefail\r: invalid option name
#
# Found when the Hailo preflight was finally run inside WSL2, which is the only
# place the Dataflow Compiler can run. The scripts had never been executed on
# Linux, so nothing surfaced it.
#
# Everything here is destined for Linux: WSL2 for the Hailo compiler and
# ArduPilot SITL, Raspberry Pi OS for the runtime, ubuntu-latest for CI. So LF
# is the repository's answer and a contributor's git config does not get a vote.

# Text files: normalise to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.cfg       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.ts        text eol=lf
*.tsx       text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the exception: it is the one thing here that only ever runs on
# Windows, and some older hosts are unhappy with LF.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Binary. Never touch these -- a "text" conversion silently corrupts them, and
# a corrupted .onnx or .hef fails at load with an error that says nothing about
# line endings.
*.onnx      binary
*.hef       binary
*.pth       binary
*.blend     binary
*.npy       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.tif       binary
*.tiff      binary
*.stl       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.tgz       binary
*.gz        binary
*.zip       binary
